{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Getting It Right"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Diverging Paths"}, {"type": "position", "content": 11}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 18}, {"type": "level", "content": "B2.2"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Describe detailed facts about events or actions in work and social contexts, in written or spoken situations"}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn10le18ob11re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " The Wh-Clause: A Review"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You can use wh-words in your sentences to form wh-clauses. The wh-words are <span class=\"italic\">who</span>,  <span class=\"italic\">whom</span>,  <span class=\"italic\">what</span>,  <span class=\"italic\">which</span>,  <span class=\"italic\">when</span>,  <span class=\"italic\">where</span>,  <span class=\"italic\">why</span>,  <span class=\"italic\">how</span>, and <span class=\"italic\"> that</span>."}, {"type": "text", "content": "When you use wh-clauses, they can come after certain verbs like:"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":1,\"columns\":4,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"explain<br/> find out<br/> decide<br/> forget\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"discover<br/> consider<br/> discuss<br/> imagine\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"realize<br/> remember<br/> see<br/> say\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"talk about<br/> wonder<br/> understand\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border\"}"}, {"type": "text", "content": "You can also use an <span class=\"strong\">object + wh-clause + infinitive</span> structure.  <ul><li><span class=\"italic\">My mother <span class=\"underline\">taught</span> me <span class=\"strong\">how</span> to sew.</span></li></ul>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "I hope you know what a great place this is! "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Do you remember which speaker talked about being convincing in an argument?"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Willingness, Annoyance, Refusal, Promises and Threats - A Review"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You can use different modals when you want to show intention, willingness, refusal, and annoyance. You can also make promises and threats using modal verbs."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":5,\"columns\":1,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"underline\\\">Willingness</span>: you use the following modals to show that you are willing to do something. <span class=\\\"italic\\\">If...will</span> in first conditional sentences can also express a polite request.<br/><br/>  <span class=\\\"italic\\\">I'<span class=\\\"strong\\\">ll go</span> with you to the doctor's if you want me to.<br/> <span class=\\\"strong\\\">If</span> you <span class=\\\"strong\\\">will cut up</span> the vegetables, then I can make the chicken.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"underline\\\">Refusal</span>: you use the modals when you don't want to do something. Other people and things can also show refusal as well. You can use <span class=\\\"strong\\\">if...won't</span> in first conditional sentences.<br/><br/>  <span class=\\\"italic\\\">My boss <span class=\\\"strong\\\">will not give</span> us a holiday on Boxing Day.<br/> The bus <span class=\\\"strong\\\">won't start</span> because something is wrong with the engine.<br/> <span class=\\\"strong\\\">If</span> Luis <span class=\\\"strong\\\">won't come</span> to the party with me, I'll ask Jorge.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"underline\\\">Intention</span>: this means that you want to do something. You use the following modals to express your purpose or aim.<br/><br/>  <span class=\\\"italic\\\">I <span class=\\\"strong\\\">will send</span> the email now.</span> (decided at the moment of speaking)<br/> <span class=\\\"italic\\\">I'<span class=\\\"strong\\\">m going to spend</span> my Christmas vacation in Barbados. </span> (decided before the moment of speaking)<br/> <span class=\\\"italic\\\">I <span class=\\\"strong\\\">would like to study</span> medicine at university.</span> (would like + infinitive)<br/> <span class=\\\"italic\\\">I <span class=\\\"strong\\\">want to buy</span> a swimsuit at the mall later.</span> (want + infinitive)\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"underline\\\">Promises</span>: you can use the following when you make a commitment to do something in the future.<br/><br/>  <span class=\\\"italic\\\">I <span class=\\\"strong\\\">will call</span> you as soon as I get home.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"underline\\\">Threats</span>: use these modals when you want to threaten people or show that something negative will result.<br/><br/>  <span class=\\\"italic\\\">I <span class=\\\"strong\\\">will tell</span> your wife that you cheated on her.</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "So, Nancy, if you will allow me to ask, I'd like to know your thoughts about the Toastmaster's meeting."}, {"type": "example", "content": "No, I won't come back. "}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "toastmaster"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a person who speaks in front of a large group"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: If you will allow me to ask, I'd like to know your thoughts about the Toastmaster's meeting."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le18ob11aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " These are words you use when you give your opinion about a Toastmaster's club meeting."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "public speaking"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the action of talking in front of a group of people in a formal setting"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: In my view, it provides an opportunity to practice public speaking and you learn a lot by listening to the other speeches."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le18ob11aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "master of ceremonies"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the person who runs a formal event "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  The master of ceremonies ran the meeting very well."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le18ob11aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "for pete's sake"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "this is crazy"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  For pete's sake!  That was too much."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le18ob11aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "procrastinator"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a person who procrastinates (waits until the last minute to do something)"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Do you know why he is a procrastinator? I think it's because he doesn't like doing the things he has to do."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le18ob11aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "the last minute "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "when no more time is left"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: When I was a student, I would always do things at the last minute.  "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le18ob11aud06"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "speaker"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a person who speaks at a public event"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Do you remember which speaker talked about being convincing in an argument?  "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le18ob11aud07"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Think of something you used to do but you don't do anymore."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Think of things your friends or family members used to do, but they don't anymore."}, {"type": "text", "content": "With a partner, discuss how you and the people you know have changed."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Use the modal <span class=\"italic\">would</span> and the Past Continuous tense for expressing past habits."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Discuss what you do now that you didn't do before."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I discuss things I used to do using appropriate grammar."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I talk about the past habits of my friends and family members using appropriate grammar."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I say what I do now that I didn't do before."}]}], "labs": [{"_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"type": "has_nav", "content": true}, {"type": "has_exercise_controls", "content": true}]}], "stimuli": [{"_data": [], "template_override": 1, "type": "welcome", "contents": [{}], "id": 0}, {"id": 1, "type": "audio", "title": "", "_data": [], "template_override": 1, "contents": [{"type": "slideshow", "value": {"audiosrc": "engenn10le18ob11re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn10le18ob11re2img01.jpg", "images": [{"text": "", "id": 0, "time": "0", "image": "engenn10le18ob11re2img01.jpg"}, {"text": "<span class=\"strong\">Gareth</span>: So, Tammy, if you will allow me to ask, I'd like to know your thoughts about the Toastmaster's meeting.<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Tammy</span>: It was interesting.<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Gareth</span>: Will you come back next week?<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Tammy</span>: No, I won't come back.  <br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Gareth</span>: I will be back for sure. I hope you know what a great place this is!  In my view, it provides an opportunity to practice public speaking - you learn a lot by listening to the other speeches. Do you remember which speaker talked about being convincing in an argument?  Was it the first or the second? He talked about using analogies.<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Tammy</span>: Yeah, he was very dynamic.", "id": 1, "time": "100", "image": "engenn10le18ob11re2img01.jpg"}, {"text": "<span class=\"strong\">Gareth</span>: Then there was the speech on the art of compromising. She was giving some helpful pointers, don't you think?  I really believe it's hard to make compromises when I'm feeling angry.<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Tammy</span>: I didn't like the speech about procrastinating. I found myself disagreeing with the things that he had been saying.  Do you know why he is a procrastinator? I think it's because he doesn't like doing the things he has to do. <br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Gareth</span>: I don't know whether I should follow his example or not. I used to be a procrastinator, too.  When I was a student, I would always do things at the last minute.", "id": 2, "time": "36500", "image": "engenn10le18ob11re2img03.jpg"}, {"text": "<span class=\"strong\">Tammy</span>:  Students will be like that. I liked the speech by the woman who went to China. I can't remember if I she went to Beijing or Shanghai. I would really like to have an experience like that.<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Gareth</span>: I will go with you. The guy who was backpacking in Chile had an incredible story. I was wondering where he got this story from. <br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Tammy</span>: Remember the strange woman who didn't want to leave the stage? The master of ceremonies had to say: \u201cIf you won't leave now, I will ask for a security guard!\u201d  <br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Gareth</span>: For Pete's sake!", "id": 3, "time": "67000", "image": "engenn10le18ob11re2img02.jpg"}]}}]}], "id": 0, "type": "scholar", "exercises": [{"questions": [], "stimuli_ids": [0], "id": 0, "type": "WLC", "img_path": "", "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can report details, reasons, or results of events or actions.  "}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can express annoyance, willingness and refusal, and make promises and threats."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can talk about past habits. "}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": " Do you think it is important to be able to speak in public? Why or why not?"}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": " Do you think joining a Toastmaster's Club would help you? Why or why not?"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Welcome"}]}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"allowed_attempts": 2, "correct_feedback": "Correct", "attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "You have 2 tries"}, {"type": "text", "content": "you have 1 attempt left"}], "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "try again"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time"}]}}, {"type": "free_header_text", "content": " Ask your partner:"}, {"type": "free_type_text_area", "content": "Let's review!"}], "template_override": 1}, {"questions": [{"_data": [{"type": "question", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}]}], "id": 0, "responses": [{"correct": 0, "_data": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}], "id": 0, "selected": 0}, {"correct": 1, "_data": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}], "id": 1, "selected": 0}]}], "stimuli_ids": [1], "id": 1, "type": "STI", "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " \nAt the end of the Toastmaster's meeting, Gareth and Tammy talk about their experience. Tammy <span class=\"tool-tip\" id=\"tip_1_0\">won't </span>come back, but Gareth will.\n"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Content"}]}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"allowed_attempts": 2, "correct_feedback": "Correct!", "attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}, {"type"